  "caption": "Quinn saw a pose online, went deeper, deeper, then too deep. The hamstring filed a complaint and the wrists joined in.\n\nYoga isn't the problem. Trouble often starts when we push into end range under load, especially if you're naturally bendy, and in heated rooms that make you feel more flexible than you are.\n\nTips that may help: own the range you can control, give your wrists a break with fists, forearms or a wedge, add some strength training, go easy on depth in hot classes, and skip headstands if your neck is niggly.\n\nPain that lingers, numbness, weakness, or sit-bone pain from deep forward folds is worth getting looked at.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
